  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnering with SIDS to deliver a 75% reduction in Plastic Pollution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Establish a plastic waste baseline: Gather and analyse data on plastic waste generation, composition, and leakage pathways to understand the current plastic pollution landscape. 

2. Project future trends: Model how plastic waste and leakage may evolve over the next 10&#x2013;20 years under a &#x2018;Business as Usual&#x2019; scenario. 

3. Develop a National Action Plan: Using the Plastic Drawdown tool, create a roadmap that outlines evidence-based policy recommendations to reduce plastic pollution. 

4. Provide strategic and technical support: Offer guidance on policy design, stakeholder engagement, and communication to strengthen countries&#x2019; efforts in addressing plastic pollution. 

5. Align with international commitments: Support partner countries in leveraging its progress within the context of global environmental agreements, including the UN Global Treaty on Plastic Pollution.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner countries: Grenada, St Lucia, Papua New Guinea, Guinea Bissau,
Tuvalu</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Small Island Developing States (SIDS)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support partner countries in developing a National Action Plan (NAP) to significantly reduce plastic pollution by providing data, evidence, and strategic policy recommendations.</narrative>
  </description>
